4.1 A Lost Chance: Horizontal Expansion without Vertical Upgrading
Before turning to Hong Kong’s post-colonial era, let us assess the consequence of the particular kind of export-led industrialization undertaken in Hong Kong. As Gereffi and Korzeniewicz (1994) suggests, the way Hong Kong’s manufacturers utilized the trading and international subcontracting networks is the “buyer-driven” type in the global governance structures in global commodity chains. Local manufacturers connected to intermediate trading companies which subcontracted orders from large
